<div class="wrap prose"><h1 class="ph">What actually installs in Grok Build</h1>
<p class="lead">We install xAI marketplace plugins, plus Claude Code plugins through Grok's documented Claude marketplace support, in a throwaway sandbox with no accounts or keys. It counts only if Grok Build then lists it as installed. Latest run{% if testing.runAt %} ({{ testing.runAt | replace("T"," ") }}){% endif %}: <b>{{ ok.length }} of {{ ok.length + bad.length }}</b> installed.</p>
{% set total = ok.length + bad.length %}
<h2>What installs in Grok Build?</h2>
<p class="answer">In our latest sandbox run, {{ ok.length }} of {{ total }} plugins we tested installed in Grok Build and showed up as installed. That covers xAI marketplace plugins and Claude Code plugins added through Grok's Claude marketplace support. The full list with each install command is further down this page.</p>
<h2>Why do some plugins fail in Grok Build?</h2>
<p class="answer">Two patterns explain most of the {{ bad.length }} failures. Claude Code LSP plugins don't install in Grok Build, and some plugin names now exist in more than one marketplace, so Grok refuses until you pin one with <code>name@marketplace</code>. Each plugin's page has the log from our run.</p>
